WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.460
11 AWESOME VIDEO GAMES NOBODY PLAYED

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:11.340
There's nothing more exciting than a sleeper
hit--a video game that defies everyone's expectations

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.490
and sells like hotcakes.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.090
On the other hand, there are plenty of legitimately
great games that just gather dust on the store

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.240
shelves.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:24.890
Let's pour one out for these games that were
awesome, but just didn't sell like gangbusters.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.041
KINGDOMS OF AMALUR: RECKONING

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:30.690
Kingdoms of Amalur: Reckoning was a game that
should've done well.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.970
The game's world and story were crafted by
fantasy writer R.A.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.110
Salvatore, and the art design was courtesy
of Todd McFarlane himself.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:43.300
Amalur featured a huge world with plenty of
quests, providing over 200 hours of gameplay.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.920
Unfortunately, those 200 hours went unplayed.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:52.399
The game sat on store shelves and only sold
1.2 million copies by the 90-day mark of its

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:53.399
release.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:56.789
This might sound like an alright number, but
it's considered a failure since it needed

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.680
to sell 3 million copies to break even.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.610
Not too long after, the game's developer,
38 Studios, filed for bankruptcy not long

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:08.990
after Amalur's release, killing any chance
at a follow-up.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:09.990
GRIM FANDANGO

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:16.090
Grim Fandango is a cult classic that was published
by LucasArts, back when LucasArts was, y'know,

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.430
still a thing.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.119
It was the very first adventure game published
by the company to use 3D graphics on pre-rendered

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:25.389
backgrounds, giving the game a really unique
look.

00:01:25.389 --> 00:01:30.170
With a film noir feel, Grim Fandango made
Manny Calavera one of the more unique video

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.369
game characters in the medium's history.

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:36.209
But even after winning critical acclaim and
praise for its design and direction, Grim

00:01:36.209 --> 00:01:40.939
Fandango is considered a commercial failure,
having moved about half a million copies in

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:42.729
worldwide sales.

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:45.259
Fortunately it found new life later on.

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:51.240
In 2015, it was remastered and rereleased
for PlayStation 4, PlayStation Vita, PC, Mac,

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.859
Linux, and even Android and iOS.

00:01:54.859 --> 00:01:55.859
EARTHBOUND

00:01:55.859 --> 00:02:00.109
EarthBound is a legend among gamers, considered
by some as one of the best ever made.

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:03.849
But most people didn't actually play it when
it was released in the '90s.

00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:08.510
Known in Japan as Mother 2, some collectors
will pay almost anything to get their hands

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.189
on a physical copy of the Super Nintendo cartridge.

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:16.969
That's crazy, since the game only sold about
140,000 units in the United States, about

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:20.560
half of what it sold in Japan in 1994.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.390
Some blame its lousy showing on bad marketing.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.670
Others point to its cartoony graphics, which
gamers at the time didn't see as much of a

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:28.939
selling point.

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:33.069
But EarthBound became more popular as the
years went on and actually spawned a sequel

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:38.670
that was released in Japan in 2006, and a
Wii Virtual Console port that came out in

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.200
2013.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.200
BEYOND GOOD &amp; EVIL

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.340
Beyond Good &amp; Evil, developed by French gaming
auteur Michel Ancel, is the definition of

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.959
a cult classic.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:52.340
It received great reviews and was critically
acclaimed for its excellent graphics, storytelling,

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.010
and unique cast.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:57.840
But it suffered poor sales during its original
release in 2003.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.670
Some attribute its terrible sales to bad marketing
and the fact that it was released at a time

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:05.739
when the market was oversaturated with big
titles that overshadowed it.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.439
A remastered version was released in 2011
for the PlayStation Network and Xbox Live

00:03:10.439 --> 00:03:13.640
Arcade, so you can play it now in glorious
HD.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:18.819
Meanwhile, even though a sequel was announced
in 2008, the game has yet to materialize as

00:03:18.819 --> 00:03:22.370
of the making of this video...eight years
later.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.370
GRAND THEFT AUTO: CHINATOWN WARS

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:29.680
Grand Theft Auto: Chinatown Wars for the portable
Nintendo DS hearkened back to the Grand Theft

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.609
Auto games of old.

00:03:31.609 --> 00:03:35.599
Players controlled Huang Lee in a top-down
style adventure in his quest to cause mayhem

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:38.069
with the Triads of Liberty City.

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:42.269
Despite being part of one of the most successful
franchises in gaming, Chinatown Wars sold

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:47.430
under 90,000 units in its first two weeks
in America, making it a commercial dud despite

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.629
its amazing gameplay.

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:53.319
Maybe it was the fact that, at the time, the
Nintendo DS was mainly thought to be a mostly

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:54.860
kid-friendly platform.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:00.799
And, really, pretty much any Grand Theft Auto
game is anything but "kid-friendly."

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:02.310
JET GRIND RADIO

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:06.069
If you had a Sega Dreamcast, you probably
played Jet Grind Radio.

00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:07.400
The big problem?

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.359
Most people didn't have a Sega Dreamcast.

00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:14.689
It's too bad; with cel-shaded graphics, the
game let players rollerblade through the city

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:19.569
while performing tricks and spraying graffiti
tags on as many surfaces as possible.

00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:23.509
With enough practice, you could skate around
the city flawlessly, with a level of grace

00:04:23.509 --> 00:04:27.880
and style that most gamers could only dream
of in real life.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.970
Despite its low sales, Jet Grind Radio did
spawn a sequel and a few HD remakes.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:38.830
At the very least, the Dreamcast classic managed
to tag the hearts of players around the world.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.370
OKAMI

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:45.580
Okami for the PlayStation 2 is a major artistic
success to its diehard fans.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.520
But its sales figures reveal it to be a definitive
commercial flop.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.360
Okami followed the adventures of the sun goddess,
Amaterasu, in a beautiful, cel-shaded world

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.460
based on Japanese folklore and mythology.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.919
With gameplay inspired by The Legend of Zelda,
it was a hit with reviewers.

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:08.310
Meanwhile, it sold 200,000 copies in North
America in 2006, and only 66,000 units in

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:10.190
Japan that same year.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:15.060
Even after being re-released on the Wii and
the PlayStation 3, Okami had trouble finding

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.250
an audience.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.330
Its sales were so bad, in fact, that it literally
set a world record.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:24.890
It was named "the least commercially successful
winner of a game of the year award" by Guinness

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.629
in 2010.

00:05:26.629 --> 00:05:30.620
That's probably not a great blurb to put on
the front of your game box.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:31.620
DARK CLOUD

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:36.270
Dark Cloud blended role-playing with city-building,
a blend of gameplay styles that reviewers

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.379
loved.

00:05:37.379 --> 00:05:41.759
Even still, it performed poorly when it was
launched on the PlayStation 2 in Japan back

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:43.310
in December 2000.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.660
Fortunately, the game did much better after
being released to Western audiences.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:51.940
And it might still find more fans going forward,
since Dark Cloud was released on the PlayStation

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:56.440
Network for PlayStation 4 in December 2015.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.370
MAX PAYNE 2: THE FALL OF MAX PAYNE

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.280
Why didn't Max Payne 2 sell well?

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.159
The first game was enough of a hit to warrant
a sequel, and the second installment earned

00:06:05.159 --> 00:06:06.770
great reviews.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:10.639
But whatever the reason, Max Payne 2: The
Fall of Max Payne sold terribly.

00:06:10.639 --> 00:06:15.320
It might as well have been called Max Payne
2: The Fall of Take-Two Interactive's Earning

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.599
Forecasts.

00:06:16.599 --> 00:06:21.449
The poor performance at retail might have
made the process of getting Max Payne 3 a

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:22.449
greenlight.

00:06:22.449 --> 00:06:26.379
Fortunately, the third game in the series
managed to right the ship, selling four million

00:06:26.379 --> 00:06:28.700
copies in its first year.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.259
VALKYRIA CHRONICLES

00:06:30.259 --> 00:06:34.849
There are few games as pretty and as addictive
as Valkyria Chronicles for the PlayStation

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:36.039
3.

00:06:36.039 --> 00:06:40.569
This strategy role-playing game had great
visuals, memorable characters, and a wartime

00:06:40.569 --> 00:06:43.030
backdrop that hooked players.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:47.960
Its sketchbook-style aesthetic brought a classic,
old-world feel to the world, which was loosely

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.410
based on pre-World War II Europe.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:56.260
Despite its positive reviews, Valkyria Chronicles
didn't have stellar sales numbers.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:00.979
It saw a sales boost after a price cut, but
it was never considered a commercial success.

00:07:00.979 --> 00:07:06.979
Luckily, its PC port sold very well on Steam,
moving about 650,000 copies within its first

00:07:06.979 --> 00:07:08.600
five months.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.600
SHENMUE II

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:14.611
Ryo Hazuki continued his search for revenge
in Shenmue II, a Sega game released for the

00:07:14.611 --> 00:07:16.720
Dreamcast in 2001.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.080
The game took place in China, meaning players
would get to explore a denser, more urban

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.280
environment.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:26.760
Shenmue II got stellar reviews...but like
lots of other Dreamcast games, sales didn't

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.990
reflect its positive reception.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.460
Two years after it was released, it had only
moved a paltry 100,000 copies.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.270
A lucky hit, Shenmue II was not.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:43.330
Then again, nearly 70,000 dedicated fans pledged
over $6.3 million to Kickstarter to make Shenmue

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.349
III a reality.

00:07:45.349 --> 00:07:50.139
That made the project the most funded video
game in Kickstarter history as of 2015.

00:07:50.139 --> 00:07:53.750
Will that be enough to help the franchise
come back for good?

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:54.750
Time will tell...

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:55.750
Thanks for watching!

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:59.629
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw, and leave

00:07:59.629 --> 00:08:03.409
us a comment to tell us your favorite video
games that should've made the list.

